WEBVTT

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:09.980
Takuya, your history is carved
into the Tree of Vrinda.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:18.400
Creating history means traveling
through infinite possibilities.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:25.050
Not a single thing you've
done is without meaning.

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:31.680
Events that are bound by
the laws of causality flow like a river,

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:34.470
in accordance with their event elements.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:39.180
Even time itself cannot break this law.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.190
At least, that's what I thought.

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:44.710
Until I learned of their existence.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.810
Our time is almost up.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.910
Takuya, we will see each other again.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:56.290
It's been decided by the weight of events,
the momentum of the event elements...

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.530
If you prefer a more
literary phrasing, it is "fate."

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:39.010
"Episode 14: The Transfer Student's Friend"

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.220
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.050
Now tell me about you.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.270
About me? There's nothing to say, really.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:54.640
Oh, right. In this parallel world
we barely know each other.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:56.400
Is there a problem?

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.030
No, nothing.

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:01.180
First, let's get to know 
each other, Kanna-<i>chan</i>.

00:03:01.660 --> 00:03:05.240
Look! Arima's hitting 
on Iron Mask over there.

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.490
She's got this kind of weird
sexiness about her, doesn't she?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.810
Yeah, I think I get it.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:18.800
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:21.720
What are you plans for the day?

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:24.230
I need to talk to Takeda-<i>sensei</i>.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:25.680
And after that?

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.490
Nothing, really.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.550
Um... What are your hobbies?

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:31.980
I don't have any.

00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:33.450
Favorite singer?

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.560
I don't listen to music.

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.310
Well, you've got a favorite food, right?

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.480
Not really.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.560
So what do you like?

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:44.890
Green... I like plants.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.950
I thought you liked the ocean.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:50.280
You know. I saw you watching it before.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.060
I don't like the ocean.

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.310
That's just my responsibility.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:58.470
Responsibility?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.550
What's wrong?

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.540
Nothing...

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.450
Eriko-<i>sensei</i>'s skipping school again.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.660
Kanna-<i>chan</i>? What's wrong?

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:23.840
You've got a terrible fever!

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.920
She's sweating really bad...
I need to do something.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:35.170
Damn it, where did that truant teacher go?

00:04:39.880 --> 00:04:43.180
Kanna-<i>chan</i>... I'll wipe
the sweat off your body!

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.660
I won't look! I won't look, so forgive me!

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:49.890
This is for purely medical reasons...

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:52.080
I don't just want to get you naked...

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.330
As soft as fresh pudding...

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.000
S-Sorry!

00:05:00.650 --> 00:05:02.680
I need to keep my eyes open after all!

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.310
Do you have a cold?

00:05:40.310 --> 00:05:41.710
You were sweating really badly.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.890
Sometimes I get these fevers...

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:48.310
Lately it's happening more and more.

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:50.630
Don't get up yet.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.040
Can we talk for a little while?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:57.650
Go ahead.

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:01.330
I feel like I've seen your
necklace somewhere before.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:04.130
But I can't remember.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:08.330
Maybe it's what they
call "déjà vu" in psychology.

00:06:09.130 --> 00:06:12.190
Maybe it was someplace my dad took me.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:16.400
When I was a kid he used to drag me all over.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.890
Your dad passed away, right?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.520
I'm sorry.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:26.560
He was a lunatic who
just called himself a historian.

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:28.640
There's no reason to feel bad.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.000
I see.

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.660
Hatano and Arima!

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.040
If you're already together, 
that saves me time.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.620
Jeez, where the hell were you?

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:44.800
I had to do something
really naughty to treat her fever!

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:46.200
What?

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:48.790
What do you want to talk to us about?

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.860
Oh, well...

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.650
Um, Yuki-<i>kun</i>, do you know
anything about Hatano-<i>san</i>?

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:06.230
The girl who just transferred here, right?

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.420
But I don't know much about
people in the upper grades.

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:09.950
Oh, right...

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:15.660
Actually, another student from
Hatano-<i>san</i>'s old school is in the kendo club!

00:07:15.660 --> 00:07:17.060
I'll ask them.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.260
Thank you!

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:23.830
Excuse me.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:24.670
Arima-<i>kun</i>?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.380
Boss? Are you joining our club?

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.190
Yes!

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.390
Something like that...

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:32.220
Actually, I'm bringing someone with me.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.970
Hatano-<i>san</i>?

00:07:34.090 --> 00:07:35.300
Can we both join?

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:37.930
I don't understand...

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.850
Why are you bringing Hatano-<i>san</i> with you?

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:43.690
Eriko-<i>sensei</i> asked me to take care of her.

00:07:43.690 --> 00:07:45.940
She's sick, she says.

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.400
She asked you to take care of a girl?

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:53.280
There was no need for Eriko-<i>sensei</i>
to leave it up to a walking libido.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:57.030
How could you say that about
an upstanding citizen like myself?

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:01.250
Whatever. You can join.

00:08:01.250 --> 00:08:05.080
For now, you can help us 
make this... diorama...

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.340
It's well-made.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:10.340
Right?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:13.940
The terrain right here is off.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:19.060
It's just like the photograph!

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:22.170
Shimazu-<i>san</i>, how old is this photo?

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:23.690
Um...

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.020
Ten years ago?

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.260
It looks different now.

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:32.570
Sakaimachi's geology
was formed in the Cretaceous

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.310
as part of the Nakaminato group.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:39.500
But Mt. Sankaku is made
of dried limestone, like a desert.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.830
That's why it changes often
due to things like earthquakes.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:46.040
She knows a lot...

00:08:46.540 --> 00:08:47.810
Oh my...

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:53.720
Well, they say that until 15 years ago,
there was another part of Futago Rock.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:55.800
Want to go look right now?

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.630
Yeah, no sense in staying here!

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:00.310
Let's all go!

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:16.610
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.370
Don't run off on your own!

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.410
You guys need to calm down!

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:22.620
Another worker was hurt in
a lightning strike two days ago.

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.660
You want us to work on
a dangerous job site like this,

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:26.870
with no guarantees of our safety?

00:09:27.140 --> 00:09:28.030
It's dangerous here.

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:32.580
--Listen, you can't come in here--
--Call off the hauling operation.

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:34.840
You with the protesters?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.010
No.

00:09:36.010 --> 00:09:39.090
Then are you going to tell us
we angered the gods or something?

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:40.930
Another lightning strike will happen.

00:09:41.060 --> 00:09:41.930
What?

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:44.100
Lightning strikes are a natural phenomenon.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:46.020
They're not our responsibility.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.480
I'm saying this for your own safety--

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.010
If you've got a problem,
take it to a judge.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:53.770
That's how things work in this country.

00:09:54.150 --> 00:09:55.070
Who are you?

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:56.740
A human being.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:01.740
Oh, you're the slacker stepson who's
causing problems for my boss, aren't you?

00:10:01.740 --> 00:10:05.370
And you're the director
who films all that porn, right?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.790
I'm the man Geotech put 
in charge of this site.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:10.170
Make them stop!

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.840
Let me go! You'll get my suit wrinkled!

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:15.090
Are you okay?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:16.670
Toyotomi, you asshole...

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.720
I just shook her off me.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:24.560
She was holding on to my
expensive suit a little too passionately...

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.720
That's really mean...

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:30.900
Listen, Toyotomi-<i>san</i>, the girl's right.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.870
I don't like the look of those clouds.

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.840
We're calling it a day.

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.390
Wait!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:40.740
I'm sick of this job.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:43.160
This is your fault!

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:45.670
I'm busy. Goodbye!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.250
Okay!

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:56.550
Those clouds are gone
like they were never here...

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.290
You're right.

00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.750
Yuki, take Mio home.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.920
On it! What about you, Boss?

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.460
I'll take Kanna-<i>chan</i> home.

00:11:05.100 --> 00:11:06.970
You will?

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:07.780
What, is that a problem?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:13.320
Hatano-<i>san</i>, if you think he's going
to try something weird, run away!

00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:14.940
Okay, got it.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.030
I would never!

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:18.990
See you.

00:11:18.990 --> 00:11:20.070
Bye!

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.030
See you later.

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:22.090
Goodbye.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.270
Let's get those photos developed right away!

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:26.240
Yeah.

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:29.540
So um, where am I taking you?

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:30.350
This way.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:36.920
It's pretty late.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:37.830
You gonna be okay?

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.660
With what?

00:11:40.050 --> 00:11:41.340
Will your parents be mad?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.410
I live alone.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.830
You're kidding...

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.220
Thank you for your help today.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:49.700
Goodbye.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.360
Kanna!

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.980
I finally found you!

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:57.820
Good evening, Hojo-<i>san</i>.

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:02.910
You haven't called at all lately!

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.660
How about we go have some fun?

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.410
I'm sorry. I'm not feeling well today.

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:10.950
Aww, don't be like that.

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:12.620
Who the hell are you?

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:13.860
A human being.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:15.880
Kanna, let's go.

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:16.630
Hey!

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:18.800
Kanna-<i>chan</i> doesn't like that!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.310
Arima-<i>san</i>, it's okay. I'm fine.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.430
Listen, kid. Who are you?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:26.640
Shut up, pedestrian.

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.680
Who are you calling a pedestrian?

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:32.530
--I'm Kanna's--
--Hojo-<i>san</i> is someone I know.

00:12:32.980 --> 00:12:35.810
Arima-<i>san</i> is a classmate of mine.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.690
Glad to hear it.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:41.080
I thought you'd made another special friend.

00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.370
Special friend?

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.200
None of your business.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:50.540
You've got no business getting involved
in other people's private lives...

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:52.370
What?

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:54.370
Stop it, both of you!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:57.460
Let's go.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:12:58.990
Come on.

00:12:58.990 --> 00:13:01.590
Kanna, call any time!

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:03.300
I'll be waiting!

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:04.150
Arima-<i>san</i>!

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:18.020
"Hatano"

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:17.610
Come in.

00:13:18.940 --> 00:13:21.780
Oh, um... I think I'll just head home.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.590
He's probably gone.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.500
I see...

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:31.110
I'm fine.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.200
This happens all the time.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:35.330
You don't look fine to me at all.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:44.390
This is just like what
happened in the nurse's office.

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:46.740
Kanna-<i>chan</i>, where's your medicine?

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.110
I don't have any.

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.930
I'm going to rest for a little while...

00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:02.810
It's the exact opposite of Ayumi-<i>san</i>'s room.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.030
Alcohol?

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:07.280
No way...

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.330
How do you feel?

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:19.260
A lot better.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:20.670
Good.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:24.840
I'm going to take a shower.
I want to get rid of this sweat.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.260
That bastard...

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:42.890
He's still here?

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.160
No way...

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:48.490
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:50.820
Kanna-<i>chan</i>!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:56.430
Is something wrong?

00:14:56.870 --> 00:14:59.900
I heard a loud noise and
thought you might've collapsed again.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.750
If you're safe, then good. Bye.

00:15:02.750 --> 00:15:03.830
Shampoo...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:06.930
I'm out of shampoo.

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.840
There's another bottle under the sink.

00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:12.430
Okay, I'll go get it.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:19.160
Does she just not get 
embarrassed by anything?

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.350
Here we go.

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:30.050
I'll leave the shampoo here.

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.080
Thank you.

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.450
What am I doing?

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:41.430
What's this?

00:15:42.880 --> 00:15:48.300
"Deposit | Kodai Arima | 300,000 Yen"

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.450
She was getting 300,000 yen from my dad?

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:52.790
Sorry, I didn't mean to peek, but...

00:15:53.970 --> 00:15:58.350
These deposits were continuing
right up to when my dad disappeared.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:01.510
You know a lot of things.

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:05.020
About my dad. About Ryuzoji.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.580
About the correction of chaos.

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:08.720
You almost know too much.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:13.450
It seems I need to tell you everything.

00:16:14.110 --> 00:16:17.620
But I have my reasons 
why I can't do that now.

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:24.280
Kodai-<i>san</i> told me to
tell you when the time came.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:26.000
My dad did?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.890
Arima-<i>san</i>, would you like to spend the night?

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.660
Spend the night?

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:33.880
Yes.

00:16:33.880 --> 00:16:36.550
You say the craziest things.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:40.890
It's late. If you don't mind...

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:45.510
I'll head home for today.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:51.110
Have a good time?

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.290
Of course not.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.560
Were you waiting for me?

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.620
Kid, what's the deal between you and Kanna?

00:16:57.990 --> 00:16:59.950
That's what I want to ask you.

00:16:59.950 --> 00:17:04.750
For a middle-aged drunk like you,
just knowing her is a crime.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.500
Whatever.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:09.250
I just have one thing to say.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:11.470
Stay away from Kanna.

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.090
Talk to her in class, and nowhere else.

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.090
And why is that?

00:17:15.090 --> 00:17:18.550
There are some things in
the world it's better not to know.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:21.780
If you're leaving, then I guess it's my turn!

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:23.450
Wait a second.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:26.140
I just came out to get some air.

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.820
"Hatano"

00:17:39.330 --> 00:17:40.030
Yes?

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:42.310
I think I'll stay after all.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:58.210
You asleep?

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:00.700
No.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:04.650
There's one thing I want to ask.

00:18:05.600 --> 00:18:06.100
Yes?

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:10.940
Is my dad still alive somewhere?

00:18:14.530 --> 00:18:15.630
He is.

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:18.570
Thank you.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:21.390
That's all I need to know right now.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:23.230
Night.

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:25.620
Goodnight.

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:32.180
I don't need a new mother!

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:36.080
You're in love with Ayumi?
She's eight years older than you.

00:18:36.470 --> 00:18:40.260
You're planning on marrying your
student who's 20 years younger than you!

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.500
In the face of love, age difference
is worth nothing more than a squid head.

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:49.000
About your real mother...

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.080
I'll tell you everything.

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.110
Your mother, Keiko, is dead.

00:18:56.820 --> 00:18:59.460
That is a fact, carved into history.

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:04.200
But not every fact is true.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:06.700
What the hell does that mean?

00:19:07.070 --> 00:19:12.030
Takuya, history isn't a 
record of past changes.

00:19:12.540 --> 00:19:14.340
What are you talking about?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:16.710
Your mother is...

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:18.840
Dad! I can't hear you!

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:22.160
Keiko is...

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:23.850
Hey!

00:19:38.070 --> 00:19:39.400
Good morning.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:40.970
Morning.

00:19:41.860 --> 00:19:44.280
You didn't do anything last night, huh?

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.220
Did you say something?

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:50.060
Do you not find me attractive?

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:54.170
Um, well...

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:57.500
When I'm with you, I just feel weird.

00:19:57.500 --> 00:19:58.280
Weird?

00:19:58.670 --> 00:20:02.090
Like I've known you for a long time...
Like you're family.

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:07.320
Um... would it upset you
if I said you seemed like a mother?

00:20:10.770 --> 00:20:11.590
No.

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:17.730
If my dad was doing
something weird to you, I'm sorry.

00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:20.840
Kodai-<i>san</i> wasn't that type of person.

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.290
Please have faith in your father.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.460
So bored...

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:35.750
There's not much to do
until those photos are developed.

00:20:35.750 --> 00:20:37.590
Let's do something summer-ish.

00:20:37.590 --> 00:20:39.800
Define "summer-ish."

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.470
Hit on hot girls in swimsuits.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.530
Is that all you ever think about?

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:44.180
Yup!

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:48.470
But the construction means
the beach is shut down.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.190
Um...

00:20:57.230 --> 00:21:03.050
My dad has a private beach in
a resort area outside of Sakaimachi.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:05.610
That's right, your family's loaded!

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:09.700
If I ask, he'd probably 
let me use it for a day.

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:10.780
Really?

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.160
Yay!

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:17.000
Hey, if we're not near Mt. Sankaku,

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.080
you won't tell us to stay away
from the ocean, right?

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:20.650
Correct.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:22.920
Then it's settled!

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:25.260
I'll get 4 tickets ready!

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:27.650
Um, I can't...

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.160
You can't swim?

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.350
I can, but...

00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:33.550
You have no swimsuit?

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:34.720
I do have one.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.570
Then come with us!

00:21:36.980 --> 00:21:39.540
I'm kind of sick...

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:45.330
Kanna-<i>chan</i>, if that's the case,
we'll feel better if you're with us.

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.900
If you collapse again when you're
by yourself, there's nothing we can do.

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.330
You think so...?

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:54.790
Yes! We're all going to the beach!

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:57.120
Well, we won't be able to hit
on any hot girls in swimsuits, though.

00:21:57.120 --> 00:21:59.160
What were you planning?

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:03.620
I guess we may as well
enjoy this rich girl's beach!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:41.530
"Episode 15: A Summer That Won't Come Back"

00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:39.010
Episode 15: "A Summer That Won't Come Back."
